Vim Cheatcheet

Mode: Normal

h - Move cursor left

j - Move cursor down

k - Move cursor up

l - Move cursor right

dd - Delete the current line

u - Undo the last change

Ctrl + r - Redo the undone change

:w - Save the file

:q - Quit Vim

:q! - Quit without saving

:wq - Save and quit



Mode: Insert

i - Enter insert mode

Esc - Exit insert mode



Mode: Visual

v - Enter visual mode

y - Copy the selected text

p - Paste the copied text



Mode: Command-line

/pattern - Search for a pattern

:%s/old/new/g - Replace all occurrences of old with new



Additional Commands
Mode: Normal

gg - Go to the first line of the file

G - Go to the last line of the file

0 - Move to the beginning of the line

$ - Move to the end of the line

w - Move to the beginning of the next word

b - Move to the beginning of the previous word

x - Delete the character under the cursor

r - Replace the character under the cursor

ciw - Change the inner word

yy - Yank (copy) the current line

p - Paste the yanked text



Mode: Visual

d - Delete the selected text

> - Indent the selected text

< - Unindent the selected text



Mode: Command-line

:help - Open Vim help

This cheat sheet covers the most commonly used commands in Vim across different modes. Mastering these commands will significantly improve your efficiency when working with Vim.
